{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019","id":1342497,"title":"W5 announced at PDXCon 2019","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-20T04:02:44-07:00","id":1342497,"title":"W5 announced at PDXCon 2019","content":"Aside from the official confirmation, it'll apparently be published by a partner Paradox will reveal later this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:36:28-07:00","id":1342511,"title":"","content":"It's best info . something more they said?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T06:59:04-07:00","id":1342517,"title":"","content":"Not really, they just said they were excited about it and that they will be making an announcement on their partner before the end of the year.<br /> <br /> You can watch the World of Darkness panel here: <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/paradoxinteractive\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.twitch.tv/paradoxinteractive</a> You will need to go to there preveous videos and look for the &quot;Live from PDXCON Berlin - Announcement show&quot; from yesterday. You will need to scrub forwrd to around the 5:16:51 mark to get to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 10-20-2019, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T07:38:44-07:00","id":1342527,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">And now for some rampant speculation:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Looking at V5 I hope they keep the rules section and the advance system sections the same, maybe a bit more clear but the same none the less. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Vampire section will obviously become the Werewolf section but I hope that for Werewolf the section to be more Werewolf driven rather than be a port of the same mechanical stylings of Vampire.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">So for example I want to feel like i am playing a creature that has to manage its Rage but I don\u2019t want Hunger dice mechanics to be just ported over as those fit Vampire more.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Hunger is gain as you rouse your blood to use your abilities and subsides when you feed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Rage however I don\u2019t think should be gained by using your abilities it should instead partially subside by using them as you are channeling your rage into these feats. You need rage to become the murderous beast that you are. So by channeling your fury into destructive force you reduce your overall rage level and the amount of Rage dice you have. You have to let it the Wolf off its leash so to speak to calm down.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Rage could be gained though by several methods. One would be similar to the tenet system in Vampire. Instead of gaining stains you make Rage checks to see if your Rage level goes up and you gain rage dice. The tenets focus on the things the story is trying to tell in this instance; what your pack cares about. There are also some universal things that will make you make a rage check and these could also be tied to your aspen or the Warm or how long you are in combat like in MET and so on; what the Garou as a whole care about. And then you can also have convection style things that are personal to your character that cause rage checks; what your character cares about.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Balance is another thing that is present in Werewolf the balance between the triat, the balance between the self and spirit, and the balance of your rage. I think that the above system is possibly good for rage I would like to see other things as well but not on a simplistic resource management pool but by something more engrained in the system itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Gnosis could be similar to rage but less that the world triggers you but just being in the presence of the spiritual gives you gnosis and then you have gnosis checks to use it on powers and stepping sideways and the like. you need to go find Caerns and meditate or be in the spirit world to gain it and gaining it is like slaking hunger so there is a definitive this give you this much mechanic but then using it is a check so you may be able to use it more often than what your level would suggest thus allowing you to have a 5 level tracker. Also maybe having to much of it effects your ability to gain Rage so if your gnosis is too high you roll two dice when making a rage check, which could be bad since you need rage to fuel your fight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Powers and abilities could then use checks form either rage, gnosis or maybe even both to fuel them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">For your Balance with the trait this could maybe be some sort of three way tracker or slide that is governed by ned and is partially your glory as well so it affects your social rolls with spirits who knows.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1C2123\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">All I know is I am thoroughly excited for W5<br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T08:03:21-07:00","id":1342528,"title":"","content":"It depends on makers limited by White Wolf. I like Onyx Path but i wish I could see W5 made by Helmgast AB. To make the game more dirty and serious. In Kult there is already concept of Gaia that remindes pangea. And it strikes me more then in any WW book. If theme mentioned already during W5 logo announcement is still the same: war and if garou are still Gaia immunity system then Kult re-creators could be good choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T22:27:39-07:00","id":1342652,"title":"","content":"They haven't announced who is goingot have the liscense for W5 yet. It may not be OP. Some are saying FFG but I wouldn't mind OP doing it since they know the setting well and I trust their company. Plus whenever they do book we get to see where inthe processe it is all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T00:49:55-07:00","id":1342660,"title":"","content":"FFG would be risky cause they have nasty habit of abandoning the licences in unexpected moment. White wolf should prepare wise long term contract if FFG would do the W5. I loved what they did with Warhammer 40 000 games, the art, the game mechanics it was very good. Onyx Path is too political correct in my opinion to create Werewolf setting I would love to buy. I like W20 but times are different now and I don't think they could grasp the darkness the world is drowning now. Helmgast could.<br /> . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T10:08:20-07:00","id":1342741,"title":"","content":"That is true FFG does tend to try to do only games they themselves are in charge of.<br /> <br /> As for political correctness I am already primed to read a book that will have a more PC bent. This is do to the responses we have seen to previous books from Paradox in particular the V5 books. I would assume at this point they try to be as drak as they can but htey may be a bit gunshy due to those books.<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with Helmgast, so I don't how well they do dark but PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T09:33:00-07:00","id":1342958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1342660#post1342660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FFG would be risky cause they have nasty habit of abandoning the licences in unexpected moment. White wolf should prepare wise long term contract if FFG would do the W5. I loved what they did with Warhammer 40 000 games, the art, the game mechanics it was very good. <b>Onyx Path is too political correct in my opinion to create Werewolf setting</b> I would love to buy. I like W20 but times are different now and I don't think they could grasp the darkness the world is drowning now. Helmgast could.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The game that champions indigenous peoples' plights and environmental concerns? That has tried repeatedly over 25 or more years to get people to note that the plight of human groups pushed to the side by colonial policies is interrelated with said concerns, and that corporate enterprise is an awful evil? OPP is &quot;too PC&quot; to take on this task? Especially when W5 was projected to revolve around the upcoming terrible shift in climate? And several splats of the game are based on said groups pushed to the side and typically ground under a boot?<br /> <br /> The books have been talking about how the world gets warped and worsened by pollution and deliberately-inflicted human misery for nearly three decades. In fact, back in the day, a fair number of people mocked it because they thought that it was &quot;too PC&quot;. So what, if anything, would the game be if it weren't &quot;too PC&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:07:25-07:00","id":1342973,"title":"","content":"Yes. I value different things in WtA then ones You mentioned. And the Onyx Path in my opinion are too pc for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:14:58-07:00","id":1342975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1342973#post1342973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I value different things in WtA then ones You mentioned. And the Onyx Path in my opinion are too pc for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>...ok man, I'll be honest:<br /> <br /> It's fine if people get value out of different aspects of a TRPG and ignore the rest; that is the nature of these games, after all. But speaking for myself, this is getting into &quot;I play VtM but hate the blood-drinking so I retcon it out&quot; levels of questionable.<br /> <br /> Like, it's been known for years that Werewolf and Mage are the most upfront of the WoD games when it comes to current social and political issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:32:30-07:00","id":1342981,"title":"","content":"You are right. And I am afraid The Onyx Path can't handle it. <br /> This is going to nowhere. I'll stick to read about news and raw info. I'm out of writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 10-22-2019, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T05:28:17-07:00","id":1343135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1342958#post1342958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game that champions indigenous peoples' plights and environmental concerns? That has tried repeatedly over 25 or more years to get people to note that the plight of human groups pushed to the side by colonial policies is interrelated with said concerns, and that corporate enterprise is an awful evil? OPP is &quot;too PC&quot; to take on this task? Especially when W5 was projected to revolve around the upcoming terrible shift in climate? And several splats of the game are based on said groups pushed to the side and typically ground under a boot?<br /> <br /> The books have been talking about how the world gets warped and worsened by pollution and deliberately-inflicted human misery for nearly three decades. In fact, back in the day, a fair number of people mocked it because they thought that it was &quot;too PC&quot;. So what, if anything, would the game be if it weren't &quot;too PC&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> PC isn't about indigenous plights or environnemental issues.<br /> <br /> If you want to know why people cringe when talking about onyx path and pc, look at the lgbt issue with Changing ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:12:48-07:00","id":1343162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343135#post1343135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PC isn't about indigenous plights or environnemental issues.<br /> <br /> If you want to know why people cringe when talking about onyx path and pc, look at the lgbt issue with Changing ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;eyebrow raise&gt; No, I'd say indigenous peoples' plights are indeed a part of 'political correctness', as part of their situation is how they're treated, and have been treated, by the dominant cultures (like the offensive name of a certain US sports team).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T07:16:47-07:00","id":1343164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343162#post1343162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &lt;eyebrow raise&gt; No, I'd say indigenous peoples' plights are indeed a part of 'political correctness', as part of their situation is how they're treated, and have been treated, by the dominant cultures (like the offensive name of a certain US sports team).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How so? Political correctness is about specific avoidance of anything that can be perceived as marginalizing or insulting toward a group. Saying that indigenous people have it bad is not avoiding anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T08:46:53-07:00","id":1343188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343164#post1343164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> How so? Political correctness is about specific avoidance of anything that can be perceived as marginalizing or insulting toward a group. Saying that indigenous people have it bad is not avoiding anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>To some, it very much is even to mention it or make it a big plot point like in WtA. Some see political correctness as discussing anything that puts blame on western people.<br /> <br /> As for the Changing Ways LTGBA+ issue, it was not PC. Heck, I'd say the way the metis section discusses homosexuality among the garou is more insulting than anything. It isn't &quot;Garou of this tribe see homosexuality between two garou as this&quot; it was &quot;Hey look! They gay! Gay Gay GAY!&quot; which really bothered me when reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T14:08:07-07:00","id":1343273,"title":"","content":"PC has always been something of a pejorative... it's just the shift from a left/progressive internal critique of those that are overly dogmatic or focused on establishment/status quo politics, to the shift to an external critique on the right towards the left in general.<br /> <br /> Though really, regardless of usage, I will hold up Beast the Primordial as exhibit A that Onyx Path is more than willing to take some serious risks along these lines.<br /> <br /> Also, lets not forget that W20 Changing Ways was supposed to be the capstone in Stew Wilson's run on WtA, but turned into a slog he basically admitted to phoning in because of the edits WW demanded from him drove him to give up on his last book. It really shouldn't be anything other than a warning of one of the pitfalls of Paradox/WW's approach to licensing out supplements for the 5th edition stuff. Sometimes you get CbN5, sometimes you get W20 Changing Ways, depending on how well the Paradox team and the developer get on the same page. And licensing out the corebook itself is going to make it that much harder to make sure everyone gets on their page regardless of how well you think any given publisher can handle WtA's politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-23-2019, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T17:15:49-07:00","id":1343304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343135#post1343135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> PC isn't about indigenous plights or environnemental issues.<br /> <br /> If you want to know why people cringe when talking about onyx path and pc, look at the lgbt issue with Changing ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at ground zero for that on here and rpg.net, as were most of the other posters on this thread. There were many pages where a poster spewed out very questionable views and prejudices about the Black Furies and feminism. It didn't resemble anything about what was written about the tribe at all (or feminism, naturally), save for the entry in BotW 2nd edition that notes what Furies who dance the spiral are often like..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T17:29:03-07:00","id":1343307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343304#post1343304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was at ground zero for that on here and rpg.net, as were most of the other posters on this thread. There were many pages where a poster spewed out very questionable views and prejudices about the Black Furies and feminism. It didn't resemble anything about what was written about the tribe at all (or feminism, naturally), save for the entry in BotW 2nd edition that notes what Furies who dance the spiral are often like..</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the book itself DID start it. People just then ran with the book's (really confusing) mentality about the Furies and applied their own dislike of them onto it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Generally, though, the mentality that social issues and such do not belong in WtA makes me ponder on the games people play of it? WtA is very verstaile, but it is very open about its dislike of megacorps, racism, colonialism and abuse of natural resources. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T21:45:04-07:00","id":1343343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343307#post1343307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, though, the mentality that social issues and such do not belong in WtA makes me ponder on the games people play of it? WtA is very verstaile, but it is very open about its dislike of megacorps, racism, colonialism and abuse of natural resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> Like to be honest: if you're someone who wants to play as werewolves but don't want to get into the social and political issues that are baked into Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> Just go play Werewolf: the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T23:32:18-07:00","id":1343352,"title":"","content":"Though, be warned, Forsaken has it's own social and political issues bake into that game too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T06:32:17-07:00","id":1343396,"title":"","content":"I dislike W20 for a some of design choices. But I always assumed, V20 was the last White Wolf product and probably long in the making, and W20 was OPP and probably a bit rushed by OPP, finding it's bearing. I really liked that W20 Changing Breeds was up on google drive and everyone could comment. Some of my comments made it into the final edit. 'Rage across the world' saw not that much involvement of fans, but we saw it before it was final, told that the Den Parent was missing, and got an extra paragraph. Directly contradicting 'Guardians of the Caerns', but ... <br /> <br /> Now, after the discussion here I opened Changing Ways PDF for the first time and jumped from all mentions of 'gay' and 'homosexuallity' to see what all the fuss is about and ... argh.<br /> <br /> Why are the rage driven hypocrites suddenly all inclusive of homosexuality amongst their own kind. For that is what I read there. I mean, it would be totally okay if they accepted homesexuality between garou/human and garou/kin, even garou/wolf couples. But, one fundamental tenet of the Litany was the &quot;garou shall not mate with garou&quot; thing-y and as so many older supplements pointed out, it wasn't a rule solely existing because of Metis. Hell, it was indicated the law was older than the first metis in the quais-Metis-Breebook that was the Metis chapter of &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot;. <br /> <br /> Just like the very first thing, that caught my eye in Changing Ways (contradicting again 'Guardians of the Caern' in regards to shifting while pregnant), I get the distinct impression that W20 authors either didn't care for already established material or outright ignored it.<br /> <br /> So, it reinforces me feeling that I'm not handled as a serious reader, but just fed the opinion of another author (team), on a given subject. Would if have hurt to create sidebar and stat &quot;here we changed something from &lt;insert book&gt;, we did it because&quot;. <br /> I can only reinforce, every time, how well V20 handled sidebars with information like what will happen to the Ravnos in canon, and TB Black Furies revised, where sidebars told us &quot;hey, change to Medusa and the morphing-plague as plot hooks, not meta-plot, use them if you like.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T08:30:05-07:00","id":1343423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343396#post1343396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the rage driven hypocrites suddenly all inclusive of homosexuality amongst their own kind. For that is what I read there. I mean, it would be totally okay if they accepted homesexuality between garou/human and garou/kin, even garou/wolf couples. But, one fundamental tenet of the Litany was the &quot;garou shall not mate with garou&quot; thing-y and as so many older supplements pointed out, it wasn't a rule solely existing because of Metis. Hell, it was indicated the law was older than the first metis in the quais-Metis-Breebook that was the Metis chapter of &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I fully believe that garou would not be against homosexual relationships in general, but so openly among each other and with so little explanation to why. It also, in my opinion, is written in a very childish tone. Aside from the law actually being very sensible given the need for kinfolk, the danger of metis and garou being isolated not being good. The ahroun chapter in Book of Auspices does detail some homosexual behaviour among two ahroun, but even then it was clearly more a battlefield stress relief thing than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343396#post1343396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like the very first thing, that caught my eye in Changing Ways (contradicting again 'Guardians of the Caern' in regards to shifting while pregnant), I get the distinct impression that W20 authors either didn't care for already established material or outright ignored it.<br /> <br /> So, it reinforces me feeling that I'm not handled as a serious reader, but just fed the opinion of another author (team), on a given subject. Would if have hurt to create sidebar and stat &quot;here we changed something from &lt;insert book&gt;, we did it because&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that the changes WW demanded were a huge reason for the book being so awful at places. The lupus chapter alone has two REALLY uncomfortable parts that needed not to be there.<br /> <br /> I forever look at the Silver Fang and Wendigo sections in the metis section as proof how much the tone was shifted from the 20th edition typical. Add to it the BNS book mess that affected Changing Ways and it was a mess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:22:02-07:00","id":1343505,"title":"","content":"As the fan that inspired the W20 core book developers (who were not the developers for the rest of the W20 run) to do the Restricted/Discouraged split in Backgrounds... I reject the idea that W20 was rushed and lacking in input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:50:38-07:00","id":1343513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343505#post1343505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the fan that inspired the W20 core book developers (who were not the developers for the rest of the W20 run) to do the Restricted/Discouraged split in Backgrounds... I reject the idea that W20 was rushed and lacking in input.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there were the blog posts that let us discuss stuff like this. For me, the lupus &quot;they can learn human languages&quot; and the PureBreed clarification both were added. If it was rushed, there was no way they could have done the blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T05:18:47-07:00","id":1343561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343505#post1343505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the fan that inspired the W20 core book developers (who were not the developers for the rest of the W20 run) to do the Restricted/Discouraged split in Backgrounds... I reject the idea that W20 was rushed and lacking in input.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is personal experience. Sure, there were forum discussions back then, and with disbelieve I read an early excerpt that stated homid in homid form would not loose gnosis when touching silver. People pointed out to me, that the section was copied from revised core and were correct. However I stated, that such an information should be with the gnosis or silver rules in the rules section, not in the homid write-up in the fluff section.<br /> <br /> Same is with &quot;Using Rage&quot; (Rage section) which names some things Rage can do, without referencing to &quot;Spending Rage&quot; (Combat section), that has partly new and partly redundant information and shall not be confused with &quot;Spending Rage&quot; (action section) which has redundant information, too. <br /> <br /> Also, possibly there were more excerpts to read, and I missed them, but had I read their change to &quot;cubs are kinfolk, when pre-change&quot; I had pointed out that then the &quot;baptism of fire&quot; needs re-working instead of Copy&amp;Paste from revised.<br /> <br /> Community collaboration was, irrc, a big theme back then, probably because Paizo did well with Pathfinder. And OPP was, in my recollection, still getting it's bearing. But, I believe, the level of cooperation was biggest on W20 Changing Breeds, and never returned to that level.<br /> <br /> Well, as far as I remember, we had no &quot;lead-storyteller&quot; before. And I'm not sure how much I like the way Martin Ericsson wants the WoD to go.<br /> <br /> In any case, V20 and TB Black Furies revised made me feel, in no small way due to the sidebars explaining the changes to the Setting, as if the respective book was made to meet my needs as player/ST - hence I felt appreciated. I miss that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-25-2019, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T18:15:44-07:00","id":1343692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343304#post1343304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was at ground zero for that on here and rpg.net, as were most of the other posters on this thread. There were many pages where a poster spewed out very questionable views and prejudices about the Black Furies and feminism. It didn't resemble anything about what was written about the tribe at all (or feminism, naturally), save for the entry in BotW 2nd edition that notes what Furies who dance the spiral are often like..</div> </div> </div> </div>1000% this. (I'm alive, I've just been busy with the life change of Maiden to Mother...)<br /> <br /> Changing Ways was a mess and I really want to know what was NuWolf's influence and what was Onyx Path as up to that book the material was great. I was thrilled to find that Ericsson got the boot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T18:54:05-07:00","id":1343695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343273#post1343273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PC has always been something of a pejorative... it's just the shift from a left/progressive internal critique of those that are overly dogmatic or focused on establishment/status quo politics, to the shift to an external critique on the right towards the left in general.<br /> <br /> Though really, regardless of usage, I will hold up Beast the Primordial as exhibit A that Onyx Path is more than willing to take some serious risks along these lines.<br /> <br /> Also, lets not forget that W20 Changing Ways was supposed to be the capstone in Stew Wilson's run on WtA, but turned into a slog he basically admitted to phoning in because of the edits WW demanded from him drove him to give up on his last book. It really shouldn't be anything other than a warning of one of the pitfalls of Paradox/WW's approach to licensing out supplements for the 5th edition stuff. Sometimes you get CbN5, sometimes you get W20 Changing Ways, depending on how well the Paradox team and the developer get on the same page. And licensing out the corebook itself is going to make it that much harder to make sure everyone gets on their page regardless of how well you think any given publisher can handle WtA's politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out changing way did not endorse anti vaxxers. It simply said &quot;some garou are against vaccines&quot; it didnt say that they are cool or that you should play them<br /> Depiction is not endorsement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T00:27:53-07:00","id":1343729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343692#post1343692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Ways was a mess and I really want to know what was NuWolf's influence and what was Onyx Path as up to that book the material was great. I was thrilled to find that Ericsson got the boot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only things we have had confirmed are the changes in chapter 1, as the writer highlighted what was added from their submitted text, and Stew later confirmed the additions came from WW. That confirmation implied more notes from WW, but didn't detail them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343695#post1343695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out changing way did not endorse anti vaxxers. It simply said &quot;some garou are against vaccines&quot; it didnt say that they are cool or that you should play them<br /> Depiction is not endorsement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea why you're quoting me about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T08:23:17-07:00","id":1343775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1343729#post1343729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only things we have had confirmed are the changes in chapter 1, as the writer highlighted what was added from their submitted text, and Stew later confirmed the additions came from WW. That confirmation implied more notes from WW, but didn't detail them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea why you're quoting me about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake sorry I thought I saw a post talking about that here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T13:24:54-07:00","id":1343848,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the biggest problem with the Changing Ways additions and the general nuWW mess was that it had no true meat to it. I mean, yeah, Furies and Talons kidnap homids for breeding, but not only is it very out of their traditions, but it also has no depth to it. Shock is like a jump scare, it is more a reaction than a deeper feeling of dread.<br /> <br /> <br /> WtA certainly had traditional werewolf horror in it, but mostly its horror comes from the hopeless feeling of not being able to DO anything to fix the world now. Thus a lot of it is focused on the horror of urban decay, pollution, racism, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thus, if I were to write W5, I'd focus on these things.<br /> <br /> <br /> What does it mean for garou of America, when school shootings have become so commonplace that some schools have armed guards. How often do the Glass Walkers have to cover up First Changes that happened during a school shooting? How many of those cubs end up as BSDs thanks to the armed pentex guards?<br /> <br /> <br /> How do the Fenrir deal with the sudden rise of alt.right? What if some of their cubs start trying to reform the Swords of Heimindal?<br /> <br /> With growing gender politics, do the Black Furies face internal strife as they argue what makes a woman?<br /> <br /> With the number of refugees coming to Europe, changing breeds of various ilk start to Change in very strange places. How do the local tribes deal with them? How are the Nation and their Fera cousins dealing with the human smuggling becoming a larger problem that might feed the Wyrm?<br /> <br /> There are more deadly hurricanes and tsunami and fires, more and more common each year. What do the local spirits feel about it? Are some starting to get used to having their aspects become stronger?<br /> <br /> These are just a few things that have not only meat in them but also go into the horror of WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T01:25:29-07:00","id":1344148,"title":"","content":"I would agree with the themes, but while investigating such horrors, the garou should occasionally be able to make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T02:42:56-07:00","id":1344158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1342497-w5-announced-at-pdxcon-2019?p=1344148#post1344148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree with the themes, but while investigating such horrors, the garou should occasionally be able to make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, I just threw those as examples of using IRL modern issues in WtA terms without making it into a huge mess.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd really love to see, inspired by Children of Gaia revised, is the divide of Children of Gaia to ennuied cliaths and burned out elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}